    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i hear you, but talking about \"finding joy in the here and now\" feels like a bit of a distraction from the actual math. if we look at it purely through the lens of thermodynamics, everything is just trending toward disorder and nothingness. i feel like i'm just spending a massive amount of mental and emotional energy to maintain this \"structure\" of a life, but the universe is literally designed to tear it all down. it feels like a waste of resources to keep trying when the end state is already determined. doesn't it seem more logical to just accept the entropy instead of fighting it so hard?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
